PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The critical correlation $c^*$ is determined by setting the expected synaptic weight change to zero at steady state, balancing the pre- and postsynaptic accumulator covariance against the baseline drift. Incorporating the causal exponential filter overlap yields a covariance term scaled by $(\tau_u + \tau_v)^{-1}$, while the baseline drift contributes $(\phi \mu + \rho) S$. Rearranging the zero-drift condition into the form $c^* = \frac{\kappa S - 1}{S - 1}$ uniquely defines $\kappa = -(\tau_u + \tau_v)\left(\mu + \frac{\rho}{\phi}\right) = (\tau_u + \tau_v)\left(-\frac{\rho}{\phi} - \mu\right)$, which is strictly positive under the requisite baseline depression regime $\rho < -\phi \mu$.
}

